  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22549009"
    description: "Archived snapshot of this software on Zenodo"
abstract: >-
  A collection of finite-difference solvers for classical fluid mechanics and
  heat transfer problems, each verified against an independent reference: a
  closed-form analytical solution, a published benchmark (Ghia, Ghia & Shin,
  1982), or a theoretical order of accuracy. Includes the Blasius laminar
  boundary layer, the lid-driven cavity (incompressible Navier-Stokes),
  two-dimensional steady conduction, one-dimensional transient conduction,
  and heat-exchanger sizing via the effectiveness-NTU method, backed by a
  35-test automated verification suite.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - heat transfer
  - finite difference methods
  - verification and validation
  - boundary layer theory
  - conduction
  - Navier-Stokes
